      "source_text": "Many patients possess social support but lack medical recognition. I possessed increasing medical recognition while losing social support. At first this appeared to be a contradiction. Later I realized it was a paradox. Both realities were true. Both patients were suffering. Both patients were searching for the same thing: stability."
    },
    {
      "path": "audio/patients_paradox_excerpt_02.wav",
      "sha256": "08dfee86424fcf3c2cd8158db324022b7ae68141873914a2a91f6a717e3200d5",
      "source_text": "Reality still has to be held by people — a family, a physician, a reviewer. What Neverlost adds is a way to carry that reality faithfully between them."
    }
